`assets/character/` includes the character sheets, portraits, wallpapers, the
Codex pet sprite sheet, the pet manifest, and the character cursor theme.
`assets/orca/aura-theme.css` is configuration and stays under the MIT license,
even though it points at the two excluded backgrounds.

The AuraSD cursor directories also contain some function glyphs adapted from
KDE Breeze Cursors. Those glyphs stay under the LGPL and GPL notices in
`assets/cursors/`. The notices themselves (`BREEZE-CURSORS-NOTICE.txt`,
`GPL-3.0.txt`, and `LGPL-3.0.txt`) are third-party license texts. The Aura
frames in the same themes are fan art and are not MIT.

Aura Symbols

The Aura Symbols font is original, but it is excluded from the MIT license.
The U+E9A2 head glyph depicts Aura (horns and twin braids). The scales and
sword glyphs are in the same font file, so the file is not offered under MIT.
The same personal, non-commercial fan terms above apply to:

- themes/sddm/aura-soulflame/AuraSymbols.otf
- docs/media/aura-symbols.png

